Section 571.030 (RSMo): 1. A person commits the offense of unlawful use of weapons, except as otherwise provided by sections 571.101 to 571.121, if he or she knowingly: (12) Transports or stores a loaded, concealed firearm in a motor vehicle and outside of a locked container or locked trunk.
Section 571.030 (RSMo): Subdivisions (1) and (12) of subsection 1 of this section do not apply to any person nineteen years of age or older or eighteen years of age or older and a member of the United States Armed Forces, or honorably discharged from the United States Armed Forces, transporting a concealable firearm in the passenger compartment of a motor vehicle, so long as: (1) Such firearm is otherwise lawfully possessed; and (2) One of the following: (a) If the firearm is a handgun, the firearm is under the direct control of the person carrying the firearm; (b) The person is also in possession of an exposed firearm or projectile weapon for the lawful pursuit of game; (c) The person and motor vehicle are in the person's dwelling unit or upon premises over which the person has possession, authority, or control; or (d) The person is traveling on a continuous journey peaceably through this state.
Section 571.030 (RSMo): 8. A person who commits the offense of unlawful use of weapons under: (2) Subdivision (1), (6), (7), (8), or (12) of subsection 1 of this section shall be guilty of a class B misdemeanor, except when a concealed weapon is transported or carried onto any private property whose owner has posted the premises as being off-limits to concealed firearms by means of one or more signs displayed in a conspicuous place of a minimum size of eleven inches by fourteen inches with the writing thereon in letters of not less than one inch, in which case the penalties of subsection 2 of section 571.107 shall apply;
